  - name: Weblogic Socket Open Count
    detail: The socket count for weblogic has exceeded a threshold of 850
    fluxfile: flux/wl_open_sock.flux
    severity: 1
    threshold: 850
    comparison: gt
    tags: 
      - host
      - _field
      - _measurement
    interval: 120
    target: xapi
    action: | 
              High open socket counts can indicate a defective weblogic server. It may also indicate unusual and protential serious
              activity. Look at haproxy stats for new connections. If that is unusally high, attempt to collect source IP addresses.
              If the incoming load seems normal, then the high count indicates that weblogic is unable to service the connections
              fast enough. If this occurs on a single weblogic node, then it may need to be restarted. If more than one node
              is affected then a cluster-wide issue is present. That may be persistent storage, network or database. 